hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1639","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hisham and Yahya ibn Hakim—this is the narration of Yahya—both said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ja'far, who said: Narrated to us Shu'bah, from Ayyub, from Abu al-'Aliyah al-Bara', from 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr (RA), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said:

""How will you be when you remain among a people who delay the prayer from its appointed time?""

Abu Dharr (RA) said to him: ""Pray the prayer at its appointed time. Then, if you catch them having not prayed, pray with them, and do not say, 'I have already prayed, so I will not pray.'""

Bundar did not narrate the phrase: ""Pray the prayer at its appointed time.""

**CHAPTER:**"
